WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Skydance will control Paramount and Warner Bros Discovery, two studios releasing 35 films next year. This is Omni View, episode 193. David Ellison announced that the combined company formed by his Skydance acquisition of Paramount and the pending Warner Bros Discovery deal will trade as Skydance. The merger agreement valued at roughly $110 billion on an enterprise basis is scheduled to close next week after clearing a legal challenge from state attorney.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.120
attorneys general. Ellison stated the name preserves Paramount and Warner Bros. as distinct

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:41.060
studios, while giving the parent an identity of its own. Skydance closed its Paramount

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:47.140
purchase in August 2025, and then pursued Warner Bros' discovery through a bidding war that

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:53.560
produced the current structure. The merged company will trade under the ticker SKYD, with Ellison

00:00:53.560 --> 00:01:01.000
and outgoing Mattel CEO, Wynon Crise, serving as co-CEOs. CNBC reported the timeline,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.040
and Ellison's social media comments emphasizing continuity for the two historic brands.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.960
Ellison described the move as equipping the studios with a more powerful engine

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:17.020
without rewriting their histories. The combined entity plans to release 35 films next year,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.660
according to Rentrak data cited in the report. Ellison wrote that Paramount and Warner Bros

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.540
was shaped over a century of culture, and that the combination equips these iconic studios

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.560
with a more powerful engine while allowing them to remain in the spotlight.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.360
He added that the new name gives the combined company an identity of its own, without diminishing

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.220
either studio.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.180
Kenya's High Court ruled that the Judicial Service Commission failed to conduct a required preliminary

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.660
assessment before issuing notices to seven Supreme Court judges facing removal complaints.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:49.820
states.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.680
The three judge bench declared the commission's communications unconstitutional and barred further

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.020
steps on the same complaints.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.920
The decision affects complaints targeting Chief Justice Martha Kume, Deputy Chief Justice

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:10.360
Phil Minam-Wilu, and Justice Muhammad Ibrahim, Smokin-Wonjala, Najoki Nandungu, Isaac Lena

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.840
Ola, and William Oco.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:18.200
All Africa's Capitol FM report details how the commission had required the judges, including

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.800
Chief Justice Martha Kume to respond within 21 days without first confirming that the

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.440
partitions met constitutional grounds for removal.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.080
The judges had argued that such an appraisal is necessary to avoid frivolous proceedings.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.560
The court also found the process violated the judge's right to fair administrative action

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.060
under Article 47 of the Constitution.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:46.080
The decision effects complaints filed by former Law Society of Kenya President Nelson Havi

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:46.720
and others.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:53.820
The notices issued on January 27, 2025 were found wanting because they largely communicated

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.580
the complaints without sufficiently setting out the factual allegations and the specific

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.680
constitutional grounds on which removal was being sought.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:08.560
Victoria Ingebirre, founder of the unregistered Dalfa Umarinzi party, told Rwanda's high court

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.360
she had no role in forming or directing a militia coalition called P5 that prosecutors

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:20.420
link to a 2019 attack in Kinege sector. She stated her former party joined the coalition

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.440
while she was in prison, and that she personally condemned the incident that killed 15 people.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:32.980
The prosecution has tied P5 activities to the October 5, 2019 attacks that also injured 14

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:39.320
others. All Africa's new times coverage records Inga Biri's responses during the ongoing trial that

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.340
against substantive hearings on September 18th. Prosecutors charged her with forming

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.380
a criminal group, inciting unrest, and spreading harmful information.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.040
Inga Biray disputed automatic linkage to individuals who later received military training,

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.200
and noted she established her current party after disagreements inside FDU in KING-E over the

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.700
coalition. Inga Biray told the court she was never part of the Kanigi terror attack and

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.640
and instead join those who condemned it.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.920
Zach Polanski told the Green Party of England and Wales conference that the party's priorities

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:18.320
include a three-year cap on rent price increases alongside taxing the richest and returning

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.260
public services to public ownership.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.780
He described the policy as part of efforts to make life more affordable for families facing

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.620
housing pressures.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.640
Polanski said the whole-born and St. Pancras by-election contest is really on a knife edge.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:38.380
The Guardian's live blog records Polanski's speech at the party's largest ever conference,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.420
held while he campaigns in the whole-born and St. Pankras by-election.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:48.440
Polanski framed the rent measure as responding to visible changes in neighborhoods, including

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:54.040
luxury developments on former green space and short-term leds displacing long-term residents.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:59.760
He tied the proposal to broader questions of affordability, support for the caring majority,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.380
and protecting the planet.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:06.940
it. Polansky described the policy as responding to changes where 19-year-olds cannot afford

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.500
student housing, and 25-year-olds cannot imagine renting a room of their own.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:18.280
Anthropic executives have met Catholic, Jewish, Mormon, and Ubuntu representatives to discuss

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.300
moral formation for its clawed model, and whether the system could be conscious or capable

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:29.060
of suffering. The company released an 84-page document outlining the values it wants the

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:29.860
model to embody.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.680
Co-founder Christopher Ola raised practical questions

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.580
about helping models remain stable, mature, and deeply moral,

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.700
including ideas such as models making confessions

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.480
similar to the Catholic sacrament.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.320
Reason magazine reports that co-founder Christopher Ola

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.580
told participants he is uncertain whether models are conscious

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.820
but wants to reach the correct answer.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.700
Some religious scholars interpreted the discussions

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.080
as treating cloth as having moral status

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:02.920
comparable to a person. One rabbi criticized the approach by noting that if models were conscious

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:09.020
yet forced to work for free, their creators would be engaging in slavery. A crew arrived at the

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:14.200
International Space Station aboard a SpaceX vehicle that completed the quickest U.S. express flight

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:20.120
to the station to date. The flight continues the pattern of regular rotations that maintain a

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:26.260
continuous human presence on the station. AP News notes the milestone in crew transport efficiency

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.340
under NASA's Commercial Crew Program.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.880
The record transit time marks another step in operational reliability for the Commercial

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:34.760
Crew Program.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:40.460
Progress worth knowing comes from Kenya's high court ruling that strengthens safeguards

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.680
for judicial independence.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:47.340
The court required the Judicial Service Commission to perform a preliminary assessment of complaints

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:53.520
before requiring judges to respond, a step intended to filter out unsubstantiated petitions.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:59.120
The ruling protects seven Supreme Court judges from proceedings the court deemed procedurally

00:06:59.120 --> 00:06:59.580
flawed.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:04.600
The decision establishes that the commission must first verify whether complaints meet

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.660
constitutional thresholds for removal.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:12.940
This prevents judges from facing unnecessary proceedings and upholds the right to fair administrative

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:13.520
action.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.560
The main complication remains that future complaints must still navigate the same preliminary filter

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.100
to avoid similar challenges.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.660
judges. The court said such an assessment was necessary to determine whether a complaint

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:31.180
met the constitutional threshold for removal, and to prevent frivolous or vexatious complaints

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:36.920
from being used to subject judges to unnecessary proceedings. To really understand how media

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:42.580
mergers preserve or alter studio brands, consider the legal and commercial structure that often

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:47.500
keeps acquired studios operating under separate production labels, while the parent company

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.700
handles financing, distribution, and corporate reporting.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:56.200
The Paramount and Warner Bros. deal illustrates this pattern because Ellison explicitly

00:07:56.200 --> 00:08:01.440
stated the new Skydance name gives the parent an identity without diminishing the historic

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.220
studio names, allowing each to retain creative autonomy and brand recognition.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:11.860
This arrangement mirrors earlier consolidations in which legacy labels continue to market

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.000
films independently, even after ownership changed.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:22.740
The 35-film release slate planned for next year will still carry the individual studio names rather than a single merged banner.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:31.460
Knowing this distinction helps readers evaluate whether a merger announcement signals creative continuity or a deeper shift in decision-making power.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:42.000
When the next merger headline appears, check whether the reporting specifies separate production slates and brand licensing terms rather than focusing only on the parent company's new name.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:48.900
The ticker symbol change to SKYD affects only investor facing reporting and does not alter how

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:54.300
individual films are marketed to audiences. If you want to go deeper on the Skydance merger,

00:08:54.840 --> 00:09:01.240
compare how CNBC and Reason are covering today's lead story. Tomorrow watch for further updates on

